  "about": "Rules the correction list holds and refuses, and what a list does to recognized text. The worker (runtime/native/session/corrections.h) and the carrier (plugin/native/vocabulary.go) are both held to this file. refused_code_points is every code point neither side of a rule may hold: the Unicode general categories Cc, Cf, Zl and Zp, whole, as inclusive hexadecimal ranges in ascending order (Unicode 16.0.0; 15.0.0 and 17.0.0 list the same). Each validator is asked about every code point there is, on each side, and must refuse exactly these, with one exception: what was meant takes one of joiners inside a word, between two characters that are neither a space (spaces: the category Zs) nor a joiner, as a speaker's label does (spec/uid_label_vectors.json carries the same three tables). What was heard takes neither. malformed_utf8_hex is bytes that are not UTF-8: refused on either side, never mended. A side is at most 64 characters (code points), counted as the operations' input schemas count them, and so at most 256 bytes.",
